every playable candidate not explored reaches a child or `Q` along cited links, with no cycle | **`nodeSoundAt_of_covering`** (new): with sound links and every candidate `Covered`, the node is node-sound | yes; the cycle check is what makes `Covered` (an inductive, hence finite) hold |\n| step 6, children and `Q` (Cert:659–672) | each child is checked with `Q` re-derived by the reinsertion test | `searchSol_reinsert` (Theorem 3, item 11), `Exec.cons`'s side condition | yes |\n| the whole tree (Cert:674) | every node reachable, the root checked | `ExecOn.sound` / `Exec.sound`, by induction on completion order | yes |\n\n**What a Cert verdict therefore proves.** Cert's acceptance rests on the\nLean theorems exactly where Cert checks the premise the lemma needs. Two\nchecks fall short: the definite step and the better step check the code's\npremises. So a certificate in which every definite step names a\nhereditarily definite customer and every better step names a repaired\ncitation proves `mospValue > k` with no trust in the search. The proof is\n`nodeSoundAt_of_covering` at each node, then `ExecOn.sound`, then §5.1's\nchain. A certificate that uses the code's premises proves it only under the\ngap of §5.2. Strengthening Cert's two checks to the repaired premises is one\nsubset enumeration (or one matching) per definite step and per better step.\nThe checker is not changed in this loop (it is not solver code, but the\nowner's decision covers the fix as one piece).\n\n**What is not formalised.** The table is a reading, not a theorem about the\nPython checker. That Cert's code computes the quantities named in the second\ncolumn is checked by item 06, which re-implemented them from §2 and agreed\nwith the C node for node, and by the existing certificate tests. It is not\nproved.\n\n### 5.4 The check\n\n`python -m paper2.search_check --decide` takes 152 s on 28 cores and writes\n`data/search_decide_check.json`. It transcribes `codeFullFilter`,\n`repairedFullFilter` and `CodeNodeRepaired` through the item 10\ntranscriptions (`b_full`, `d_hereditary`, `b_is_repaired`). It runs the\nsearch with memo and old move (`decide_run`) at every `k` and both\n`L ∈ {0, 1}`. The repaired search is checked against the oracle. The code's\nsearch is instrumented at every expanded node, recording:\n\n- the invariant;\n- `NodeSoundAt`'s hypothesis on `Q`;\n- `NodeSoundAt` itself;\n- `CodeNodeRepaired`.\n\nThe graphs are:\n\n- every labelled graph on 1–6 vertices, with pathwidth computed by\n  layouts to 5;\n- every atlas graph on 7;\n- 3,000 random sparse and cover graphs on 8–12;\n- 4,000 augmented definite-move counterexamples on 14–17 (`better_augment`)\n  at `k ∈ {opt − 1, opt}`;\n- the two `DEFINITE_CEX` graphs.\n\n| statement | cases | failures |\n|---|---|---|\n| repaired search answer = oracle (`exec_repairedFullFilter_sound`) | 570,206 runs | 0 |\n| a repaired refutation has `k < narrowness = pw + 1` (layouts, n ≤ 5) | 6,132 refutations | 0 |\n| `CodeNodeRepaired ⇒ NodeSoundAt` at an expanded node (`nodeSoundAt_codeFullFilter_of_repaired`) | 1,781,000 repaired nodes of 1,782,100 | 0 |\n| a code run with no lost node keeps `Q` genuinely refuted (`ExecOn.sound`'s invariant) | 570,148 such runs | 0 |\n| a code refutation from a run with no lost node is genuine (`codeExec_sound_of_runSound`) | every such run | 0 |\n| a code refutation from a run passing the check everywhere is genuine (`codeExec_sound_of_repaired`) | 569,155 such runs | 0 |\n| `codeFullFilter cexGraph 6 L {2} ∅ = {0}`, `L = 0…3`, and the lost solution | pinned | 0 |\n\nWhat the code does, as opposed to what is proved:\n\n- **The code's own run reaches a lost node.** This happens in 58 of 570,206\n  code runs, all on augmented graphs (29 graphs, both `L`), all at\n  `k = opt`, never at `opt − 1`, as §5.2's argument requires. The smallest\n  example has 14 customers (`RUN_LOST_CEX`, `k = 6`): the run expands\n  `{1}`, where the filter keeps no child with a solution, and then finds a\n  solution through another branch. Every one of the 58 runs answered `sat`\n  correctly. In 26 of them the lost subtree joined `seen` and propagated a\n  non-refuted old move to its siblings. That is the cascade `Exec.sound`'s\n  hypothesis excludes, and it is visible here as 83 nodes with a\n  non-refuted `Q`. It did not change an answer.\n- **The code's filter fails the repaired check at 1,100 expanded nodes.**\n  At all but 58 of them it still kept a solution, or there was none to keep.\n- **Zero wrong answers** from the code's search in 570,206 runs. No\n  whole-instance false refutation is known, as before.\n- On `DEFINITE_CEX`, the code's run at the optimum never reaches the bad\n  state `{2}`: it finds a solution after 14–15 nodes. At `opt − 1` it\n  refutes correctly, and every node is sound for the reason in §5.2.\n\nThere are five new tests in `tests/test_search_check.py`, 52 in all:\n\n- a quick run;\n- every statement to 4 vertices, with pathwidth;\n- the Lean counterexample's filter for every `L`;\n- `RUN_LOST_CEX`: a lost node inside a real run with a correct answer, and\n  nothing lost at `opt − 1`;\n- a mutation of the checker: `CodeNodeRepaired` replaced by \"always true\" is\n  caught as `fail_repaired_not_sound`.\n\n### 5.5 Summary for the paper\n\n- **Proved, unconditionally.** The customer search is a sound decision\n  procedure for `MOSP ≤ k`, and so for `pw ≤ k − 1`. This covers free moves,\n  the memo, old move, the subset rule with its tie-break, and the definite\n  and better moves in their repaired forms, in the code's order, with any\n  `L`, any child order and any memo policy (§5.1).\n- **Proved, conditionally, for the code as it stands.** A refutation is\n  sound if its run expands only nodes where the filter keeps a solution\n  (`CodeRunSound`). It is also sound if every node passes a local check\n  (`CodeNodeRepaired`) that a strengthened certificate could carry (§5.2).\n- **Refuted.** Chu & Stuckey's Theorem 1, and their Theorem 2 in its\n  corrected form, are false as pairwise rules (§4.2, §4.4). The code\n  implements both. Bugs A and B are also refuted (§4.4).\n- **Open.** Whether the code's search ever answers `unsat` wrongly on a\n  whole instance. None is known: zero in this section's 570,206 runs, in\n  item 08's 690,000 graphs, and in the harness's 1.76 M calls.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='paper2/search_soundness.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"- §5 (item 12) states the theorem and maps each premise the certificate checker\n  verifies to the Lean lemma that justifies it.\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"- §5 (item 12) states the theorem and maps each premise the certificate checker\n  verifies to the Lean lemma that justifies it (done: the repaired search is\n  proved sound end to end, `mospValue > k` and `pw > k − 1`; the code as it\n  stands is sound under a named run-local hypothesis or a checkable per-node\n  condition; Cert's definite and better checks are the two whose premise is\n  not the one the Lean lemma needs).\"\"\"\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nold=\"\"\"**Code references** are to the tree\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"> **Theorem (item 12, 2026-10-01).** `Search/Decide.lean`: a refutation by\n> the customer search with free moves, the memo, old move and\n> `definite → subset → better`, the definite and better moves repaired, means\n> `mospValue > k` on the MOSP graph and `pw > k − 1`\n> (`exec_repairedFullFilter_mospValue`, `exec_repairedFullFilter_pathwidth`).\n> For the code as it stands, the gap is named, `CodeRunSound`: its run expands\n> only nodes where its filter keeps a solution. Under that hypothesis, or a\n> checkable per-node condition (`CodeNodeRepaired`), the same conclusions hold\n> (`codeExec_mospValue_of_runSound`, `codeExec_mospValue_of_repaired`). The\n> hypothesis fails at a node on `cexGraph` (`not_codeFilterSound_cexGraph`),\n> and the code's own runs reach such nodes on 58 of 570,206 runs, always on\n> satisfiable instances. No wrong answer was seen. §5.3 maps each check of\n> the certificate checker to its Lean lemma. Two checks, definite and\n> better, verify the code's premise rather than the repaired one.\n\n**Code references** are to the tree\"\"\"\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nwc -l lean/MOSPFormalization/Search/Decide.lean; grep -c \"print axioms MOSPFormalization.Search\" paper2/axiom_check.lean"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01ENgmSjwPakvxikqRMwSHNn":{"cwd":"/home/al/dev/MOSP"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ENgmSjwPakvxikqRMwSHNn","type":"tool_result","content":"454 lean/MOSPFormalization/Search/Decide.lean\n72","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e16c045b-e24f-404f-85ea-2e2a6ff5bc85","uuid":"c94ce8d3-24df-4037-adf3-0edc55a5986f","timestamp":"2026-10-01T00:16:12.222Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"454 lean/MOSPFormalization/Search/Decide.lean\n72","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/paper2/search_soundness.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":13,"oldLines":7,"newStart":13,"newLines":11,"lines":[" - §3 (item 06) checks every statement by brute force (done: zero failures for the fixed rules; both bad forms fail)."," - §4 (items 07–11) gives the Lean proofs (§4.1, the model and the free move, done in item 07; §4.2, the definite move, item 08: false as stated, repaired and proved; §4.3, the subset rule, item 09: sound as coded, on its own and after the repaired definite move, and its index tie-break is necessary; §4.4, the better move, item 10: its corrected form is still unsound, because it is Theorem 1 at the child, and it is repaired and proved, with the composition and Lean counterexamples to Bugs A and B; §4.5, the memo and the old move, item 11: each sound, and sound together, which settles §2.7's claim; the Python's reason for refusing the combination is a checkability point, not a soundness one)."," - §5 (item 12) states the theorem and maps each premise the certificate checker","-  verifies to the Lean lemma that justifies it.","+  verifies to the Lean lemma that justifies it (done: the repaired search is","+  proved sound end to end, `mospValue > k` and `pw > k − 1`; the code as it","+  stands is sound under a named run-local hypothesis or a checkable per-node","+  condition; Cert's definite and better checks are the two whose premise is","+  not the one the Lean lemma needs)."," "," §1–2 were written in loop0006 item 05 and contain no Lean."," "]},{"oldStart":75,"oldLines":6,"newStart":79,"newLines":21,"lines":[" > (`exec_repairedFullFilter_sound`). The inheritance test is necessary"," > (`reinsert_needs_test`, a 5-vertex path). §4.5."," ","+> **Theorem (item 12, 2026-10-01).** `Search/Decide.lean`: a refutation by","+> the customer search with free moves, the memo, old move and","+> `definite → subset → better`, the definite and better moves repaired, means","+> `mospValue > k` on the MOSP graph and `pw > k − 1`","+> (`exec_repairedFullFilter_mospValue`, `exec_repairedFullFilter_pathwidth`).","+> For the code as it stands, the gap is named, `CodeRunSound`: its run expands","+> only nodes where its filter keeps a solution. Under that hypothesis, or a","+> checkable per-node condition (`CodeNodeRepaired`), the same conclusions hold","+> (`codeExec_mospValue_of_runSound`, `codeExec_mospValue_of_repaired`). The","+> hypothesis fails at a node on `cexGraph` (`not_codeFilterSound_cexGraph`),","+> and the code's own runs reach such nodes on 58 of 570,206 runs, always on","+> satisfiable instances. No wrong answer was seen. §5.3 maps each check of","+> the certificate checker to its Lean lemma. Two checks, definite and","+> better, verify the code's premise rather than the repaired one.","+"," **Code references** are to the tree at commit `8d824d034`:"," `satisfiability/customer_search.py` (**Py**, the reference implementation),"," `satisfiability/customer_search.c` (**C**), and"]},{"oldStart":1748,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1767,"newLines":223,"lines":[" - the no-test mutation's false refutation, with its invariant violations;"," - a mutation of the checker: `inherit` replaced by \"keep everything\" is","   caught as `fail_tree_answer` and `fail_q_not_refuted`.","+","+---","+","+## 5. The theorem (item 12)","+","+`lean/MOSPFormalization/Search/Decide.lean`, namespace","+`MOSPFormalization.Search`, about 470 lines. It has no `sorry`, and its axioms","+are `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound` only","+(`../paper2/axiom_check.lean`, 37 new lines). Nothing is added to","+`Ralph_Loops/loop0006/allowed_sorries.txt`. The gap left for the code as it","+stands is stated as a named `Prop` and used as an explicit hypothesis, never","+as a `sorry`.","+","+### 5.1 The search, and what a refutation means","+","+The abstract search is item 11's `Exec G k F M S Q o M′` (§4.5.1). It covers:","+","+- the tree of free-closed states;","+- a filter `F` applied at `(S, Q ∖ S)`;","+- the memo under any policy;","+- old moves, with any inherited subset that passes the code's test;","+- any child order.","+","+A refutation is a completed run from the root, `Exec G k F ∅ ∅ ∅ none M′`.","+Item 12 instantiates `F` with the rules of items 07–11 in the code's order,","+`definite → subset → better`.","+","+**Theorem (the repaired search).** Suppose the definite move fires only on a","+hereditarily definite customer (§4.2) and the better move cites only under","+the repaired premise (§4.4), with any limit `L`. Then a refutation of `k` on","+a graph `G` means:","+","+| conclusion | Lean |","+|---|---|","+| `¬ Solvable G k ∅`: no closing order costs at most `k` | `exec_repairedFullFilter_sound` (item 11) |","+| `k < narrowness G` | `exec_repairedFullFilter_narrowness` |","+| `pw(G) > k − 1`, written `k ≤ pathwidth G` (`V` nonempty) | `exec_repairedFullFilter_pathwidth` |","+| on the MOSP graph of an instance `M` with a requirement: `mospValue M > k` | `exec_repairedFullFilter_mospValue` |","+| the same, in pathwidth form: `pw(G_M) > k − 1` | `exec_repairedFullFilter_mospGraph_pathwidth` |","+","+The chain is: `Exec.sound` (item 11), then `solvable_empty_iff` (Lemma F at","+the root, item 07), then `searchSol_empty_iff_pathwidth_add_one_le` (item 07,","+through `Complex.narrowness_eq_pathwidth_add_one`, loop0005), then","+`searchSol_mospGraph_iff_mospValue_le` (item 07, through","+`MOSPGraph.lean`'s `mospValue_eq_pathwidth_add_one`). The search runs on the","+MOSP graph. It drops customers with no product, and `mospGraph` keeps them","+as isolated vertices. They are free at the root, so nothing changes","+(§4.1.3). That remark is not formalised.","+","+### 5.2 The search as coded: the named gap","+","+The code's filter is `codeFullFilter G k L` (`BetterMove.lean`). Its definite","+move uses `close ≥ open` and its better move uses the corrected premise 4.","+**This filter is not node-sound.** On `cexGraph` at `k = 6`, for every `L`,","+it keeps only `0` at the free-closed state `{2}` (`codeFullFilter_cex`). That","+state has a solution and `cl({0, 2})` has none. Against the named property","+this is:","+","+- `CodeFilterSound G k L := FilterSound G k (codeFullFilter G k L)`, which","+  says the code's filter is node-sound at every state of one instance at one","+  `k`;","+- `not_codeFilterSound_cexGraph : ¬ CodeFilterSound cexGraph 6 L`.","+","+What holds for the code is therefore conditional. The condition is the","+run-local form of node soundness. `ExecOn G k F N` is `Exec` in which every","+node the run expands satisfies `N`. Every `Exec` is an `ExecOn` with the","+trivial `N` (`Exec.execOn`), and conversely (`ExecOn.exec`). `ExecOn.sound`","+is `Exec.sound` with the filter required to be node-sound only at the","+expanded nodes (`NodeSoundAt`).","+","+| statement | Lean | status |","+|---|---|---|","+| **the gap, named:** the code's run expands only nodes where its filter keeps a solution whenever one exists, `CodeRunSound G k L M′` | `def CodeRunSound` | a hypothesis, not a proof |","+| a code refutation under the gap is genuine: `¬ Solvable G k ∅` | `codeExec_sound_of_runSound` | proved |","+| … hence `k ≤ pathwidth G`, and `mospValue M > k` on the MOSP graph | `codeExec_pathwidth_of_runSound`, `codeExec_mospValue_of_runSound` | proved |","+| the instance-wide form: `CodeFilterSound G k L` and an `Exec` run give `¬ Solvable G k ∅` | `codeExec_sound_of_codeFilterSound` | proved; its hypothesis is false on `cexGraph` |","+| **a checkable sufficient condition at one node:** if the definite move fires, its pick is hereditarily definite; if not, every customer the better move drops has *some* earlier cited survivor meeting the repaired premise (`CodeNodeRepaired`) | `nodeSoundAt_codeFullFilter_of_repaired` | proved |","+| a run of the code whose every node passes that check is sound, and gives `mospValue M > k` | `codeExec_sound_of_repaired`, `codeExec_mospValue_of_repaired` | proved |","+","+The last two rows are what a certificate would have to carry to certify a","+refutation by the code *as it stands* under the repaired theorems. Every","+definite pick would need a hereditary check, by brute force over subsets or","+by the matching of `isHereditarilyDefinite_of_matching`. Every better-move","+drop would need one repaired witness. The code's","+answer is then sound even though its filter is not, because the node check","+holds at every node the run actually visits. The check passes on 99.94% of","+the code's nodes in the run below. At the nodes where it fails, the filter","+still kept a solution at all but 58 of them.","+","+**Why the run-local hypothesis cannot be checked from the answer alone.**","+Every node the search expands is reached from the root by playable moves.","+So if the root has no solution, no expanded node has one, and every expanded","+node is node-sound for free (the one-line argument is `SearchSol.step` along","+the path). A false refutation therefore needs `Sol_k(∅)` together with a","+lost node on every branch that leads to a solution. Lost nodes inside real","+runs do happen (§5.4). In every case observed the search found a solution","+through another branch.","+","+### 5.3 What the certificate checker checks, and the Lean lemma for each premise","+","+`learning/search_certificate.py` at `0602e1b46` (**Cert**). The checker","+walks the certificate tree from the root and checks six things at each","+node. The table maps each check to the Lean lemma that justifies it, and","+says whether the premise Cert checks is the one that lemma needs.","+","+| Cert check | what it verifies | Lean justification | Cert's premise = the lemma's? |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| status (Cert:517) | the certificate claims `unsat` at `k` | the theorem's conclusion: `exec_root_sound`, then `searchSol_mospGraph_iff_mospValue_le` | yes |","+| step 1, free moves (Cert:545–556) | the listed free customers are exactly those whose `N[c]` is opened | `cl` and Lemma F: `solvable_iff_searchSol_cl`, `solvable_insert_iff_of_free` (item 07) | yes |","+| step 2, not a solution (Cert:557–561) | the closed set is not every customer | `SearchSol.done` is the only way `Sol` holds at `univ` | yes |","+| step 3, memo (Cert:562–575, 526–528) | a memo node cites a completed refutation with the same closed set; refused under old move | `solvable_iff_of_cl_eq` (key) and `Exec.sound` (genuine entries; item 11) | yes; the old-move refusal is about local checkability (`exec_fake_oldMove`), not soundness |","+| candidates and children (Cert:576–594) | children are playable candidates outside `Q`, cost `|(O(S) ∪ N[c]) ∖ S| ≤ k` | `FilterPlayable`; the child keeps the invariant, `card_opened_cl_insert_sdiff_le_of_playable` (item 11) | yes |","+| step 4, definite (Cert:602–616) | `q` playable and `close(q, S) ≥ open(q, S)`; every other playable `r` is covered by `q` | `definite_link`: `Sol(S·r) → Sol(S·q)` when `q` is **hereditarily definite** (from `searchSol_cl_insert_of_hereditarilyDefinite`, item 08) | **no**: Cert checks `IsDefinite` (`isDefinite_iff`), which `definiteMove_counterexample` shows can certify a lost node |","+| step 4, subset (Cert:617–627) | `o(d) ⊆ o(r)`, strictly or `d < r`; `d` any remaining customer | `searchSol_cl_insert_of_newlyOpened_subset` (item 09); acyclicity from `Dominates.trans` and `not_dominates_self` | yes; the tie-break is checked and needed (`noTieBreak_counterexample`) |","+| step 4, better (Cert:628–640) | premise 3 (`S ++ [r, q]` playable) and the corrected premise 4 | `searchSol_cl_insert_of_repairedBetter`: `Sol(S·r) → Sol(S·q)` under **`IsRepairedBetter`** (item 10) | **no**: Cert checks `IsBetter` (`isBetter_iff`), which `betterMove_counterexample` shows can certify a false link |","+| step 5, exhaustiveness (Cert:641–658) | every playable candidate not explored reaches a child or `Q` along cited links, with no cycle | **`nodeSoundAt_of_covering`** (new): with sound links and every candidate `Covered`, the node is node-sound | yes; the cycle check is what makes `Covered` (an inductive, hence finite) hold |","+| step 6, children and `Q` (Cert:659–672) | each child is checked with `Q` re-derived by the reinsertion test | `searchSol_reinsert` (Theorem 3, item 11), `Exec.cons`'s side condition | yes |","+| the whole tree (Cert:674) | every node reachable, the root checked | `ExecOn.sound` / `Exec.sound`, by induction on completion order | yes |","+","+**What a Cert verdict therefore proves.** Cert's acceptance rests on the","+Lean theorems exactly where Cert checks the premise the lemma needs. Two","+checks fall short: the definite step and the better step check the code's","+premises. So a certificate in which every definite step names a","+hereditarily definite customer and every better step names a repaired","+citation proves `mospValue > k` with no trust in the search. The proof is","+`nodeSoundAt_of_covering` at each node, then `ExecOn.sound`, then §5.1's","+chain. A certificate that uses the code's premises proves it only under the","+gap of §5.2. Strengthening Cert's two checks to the repaired premises is one","+subset enumeration (or one matching) per definite step and per better step.","+The checker is not changed in this loop (it is not solver code, but the","+owner's decision covers the fix as one piece).","+","+**What is not formalised.** The table is a reading, not a theorem about the","+Python checker. That Cert's code computes the quantities named in the second","+column is checked by item 06, which re-implemented them from §2 and agreed","+with the C node for node, and by the existing certificate tests. It is not","+proved.","+","+### 5.4 The check","+","+`python -m paper2.search_check --decide` takes 152 s on 28 cores and writes","+`data/search_decide_check.json`. It transcribes `codeFullFilter`,","+`repairedFullFilter` and `CodeNodeRepaired` through the item 10","+transcriptions (`b_full`, `d_hereditary`, `b_is_repaired`). It runs the","+search with memo and old move (`decide_run`) at every `k` and both","+`L ∈ {0, 1}`. The repaired search is checked against the oracle. The code's","+search is instrumented at every expanded node, recording:","+","+- the invariant;","+- `NodeSoundAt`'s hypothesis on `Q`;","+- `NodeSoundAt` itself;","+- `CodeNodeRepaired`.","+","+The graphs are:","+","+- every labelled graph on 1–6 vertices, with pathwidth computed by","+  layouts to 5;","+- every atlas graph on 7;","+- 3,000 random sparse and cover graphs on 8–12;","+- 4,000 augmented definite-move counterexamples on 14–17 (`better_augment`)","+  at `k ∈ {opt − 1, opt}`;","+- the two `DEFINITE_CEX` graphs.","+","+| statement | cases | failures |","+|---|---|---|","+| repaired search answer = oracle (`exec_repairedFullFilter_sound`) | 570,206 runs | 0 |","+| a repaired refutation has `k < narrowness = pw + 1` (layouts, n ≤ 5) | 6,132 refutations | 0 |","+| `CodeNodeRepaired ⇒ NodeSoundAt` at an expanded node (`nodeSoundAt_codeFullFilter_of_repaired`) | 1,781,000 repaired nodes of 1,782,100 | 0 |","+| a code run with no lost node keeps `Q` genuinely refuted (`ExecOn.sound`'s invariant) | 570,148 such runs | 0 |","+| a code refutation from a run with no lost node is genuine (`codeExec_sound_of_runSound`) | every such run | 0 |","+| a code refutation from a run passing the check everywhere is genuine (`codeExec_sound_of_repaired`) | 569,155 such runs | 0 |","+| `codeFullFilter cexGraph 6 L {2} ∅ = {0}`, `L = 0…3`, and the lost solution | pinned | 0 |","+","+What the code does, as opposed to what is proved:","+","+- **The code's own run reaches a lost node.** This happens in 58 of 570,206","+  code runs, all on augmented graphs (29 graphs, both `L`), all at","+  `k = opt`, never at `opt − 1`, as §5.2's argument requires. The smallest","+  example has 14 customers (`RUN_LOST_CEX`, `k = 6`): the run expands","+  `{1}`, where the filter keeps no child with a solution, and then finds a","+  solution through another branch. Every one of the 58 runs answered `sat`","+  correctly. In 26 of them the lost subtree joined `seen` and propagated a","+  non-refuted old move to its siblings. That is the cascade `Exec.sound`'s","+  hypothesis excludes, and it is visible here as 83 nodes with a","+  non-refuted `Q`. It did not change an answer.","+- **The code's filter fails the repaired check at 1,100 expanded nodes.**","+  At all but 58 of them it still kept a solution, or there was none to keep.","+- **Zero wrong answers** from the code's search in 570,206 runs. No","+  whole-instance false refutation is known, as before.","+- On `DEFINITE_CEX`, the code's run at the optimum never reaches the bad","+  state `{2}`: it finds a solution after 14–15 nodes. At `opt − 1` it","+  refutes correctly, and every node is sound for the reason in §5.2.","+","+There are five new tests in `tests/test_search_check.py`, 52 in all:","+","+- a quick run;","+- every statement to 4 vertices, with pathwidth;","+- the Lean counterexample's filter for every `L`;","+- `RUN_LOST_CEX`: a lost node inside a real run with a correct answer, and","+  nothing lost at `opt − 1`;","+- a mutation of the checker: `CodeNodeRepaired` replaced by \"always true\" is","+  caught as `fail_repaired_not_sound`.","+","+### 5.5 Summary for the paper","+","+- **Proved, unconditionally.** The customer search is a sound decision","+  procedure for `MOSP ≤ k`, and so for `pw ≤ k − 1`. This covers free moves,","+  the memo, old move, the subset rule with its tie-break, and the definite","+  and better moves in their repaired forms, in the code's order, with any","+  `L`, any child order and any memo policy (§5.1).","+- **Proved, conditionally, for the code as it stands.** A refutation is","+  sound if its run expands only nodes where the filter keeps a solution","+  (`CodeRunSound`). It is also sound if every node passes a local check","+  (`CodeNodeRepaired`) that a strengthened certificate could carry (§5.2).","+- **Refuted.** Chu & Stuckey's Theorem 1, and their Theorem 2 in its","+  corrected form, are false as pairwise rules (§4.2, §4.4). The code","+  implements both. Bugs A and B are also refuted (§4.4).","+- **Open.** Whether the code's search ever answers `unsat` wrongly on a","+  whole instance. None is known: zero in this section's 570,206 runs, in","+  item 08's 690,000 graphs, and in the harness's 1.76 M calls."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/al/dev/MOSP/paper2/search_soundness.md"]}}}
